name issue_372_outage_interruption_count_seed10
describe Seed-10 copy for #411 D8 (libwebrtc loses about 9 % here against 5.6 % on seed 1). A 3 s outage that starts on a round time (5 s): the audio is silent for 3 s and the bench must count one interruption of about 3 s (issue #372). Seed 1 used to report none (longest 40 ms, concealed 8.0 %) because the bench counted concealment by the pull's operation, and NetEq plays leftover expanded samples on Normal pulls. Counted from concealedSamples and concealmentEvents as libwebrtc's StatisticsCalculator does, seeds 1-5 read 1 interruption of 2976-2980 ms and 10.0-10.2 % concealed.
duration 30s
seed 10
at 0s capacity=2Mbps delay=40ms
at 5s down
at 8s up
expect audio.interruptions == 1
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms > 2900
expect audio.interruption_ms < 3100
expect audio.concealed_pct > 9.5
